  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Church leaders to engage in effective advocacy in the IMBISA region</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building strategic relationships and penetrating regional spaces to influence with effectiveness is a priority for the Church to bring transformative change. In line with this priority, the Church seeks to enhance its interaction with the regional institutions, mechanisms and processes in the IMBISA region. The proposed project therefore aims to strengthen IMBISA Bishops&apos; engagement with regional political bodies, mechanisms, platforms as well as enhance wider collaboration with other Regional Faith Based Organizations, and other civic organizations that promote the common good. These efforts will amplify the Church&apos;s voice on issues that bring justice to those facing violence, poverty, and discrimination including vulnerable groups such as children, women, boys, and girls.</narrative>
  </description>
